# ProxiSpeak frontend — build-time variables (Vite)
#
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) before `npm run build`. Vite inlines these into
# the JavaScript bundle, so treat every value here as PUBLIC.
#
# Backend/server variables (SESSION_SECRET, MONGODB_URI, TURN_SECRET, ...) live in
# server/.env.example and must never be placed in this file.

# API base for the account endpoints, room tokens and ICE servers.
# Leave empty for a same-origin deployment (recommended): the dev/preview server
# proxies /api and production is expected to serve assets and API from one
# origin. Set only when the API genuinely lives on another host, and then add the
# frontend origin to CLIENT_ORIGIN on the server.
# VITE_API_URL=

# Socket.IO endpoint. Empty means same origin. The Vite config defaults local
# development builds to http://localhost:4000.
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=

# Join code for closed pilot deployments. WARNING: Vite inlines this into the
# public bundle, so it is a weak gate, not a secret. Accounts are the primary
# access control; leave this unset unless the server also sets JOIN_CODE.
# VITE_JOIN_CODE=
